llm_negotiation/runs/rf31_*/screening/**/pair_interactions.jsonl
llm_negotiation/runs/rf31_*/screening/**/trajectory.csv
# RF-18's rule-set evaluation runs (issue #74), the same way: each run's config.json, outcome.json
# and measures.json ARE tracked (the verdicts come from measures.json); the rest, events.jsonl too
# (44 MB over round 1's 150 runs), is rebuilt by running the experiment again with --overwrite
# (rule-set-evaluation.md, section 5).
llm_negotiation/runs/rf18_*/runs/**/events.jsonl
llm_negotiation/runs/rf18_*/runs/**/interactions.jsonl
llm_negotiation/runs/rf18_*/runs/**/pair_interactions.jsonl
llm_negotiation/runs/rf18_*/runs/**/trajectory.csv
# RF-35's crowd-encounter replays (issue #117): each replay reruns a 50- or 100-person flow, and its
# interaction logs come to 1.9 GB over 72 sessions. Each replay's config.json, outcome.json,
# events.jsonl and trajectory.csv ARE tracked (the viewer and outcomes need no more); the two
# interaction logs are rebuilt from the session records (`python -m negsim.resolution.replay`).
llm_negotiation/runs/rf35_crowd_encounters/replay/**/interactions.jsonl
llm_negotiation/runs/rf35_crowd_encounters/replay/**/pair_interactions.jsonl
